# A numeral can take the annexed noun with no "n": "deg ṛebɛa wussan".
# Dallet states it for ṛebɛa (p. 703); the other numerals from one to ten follow the same order
# by analogy, and they need a native answer. ṛebɛin (40) puts "n" before its noun (same page).
# Dallet 1982, Dictionnaire kabyle-français, p. 703 (dallet_1982_kf_p702-703_larebea_mercredi.png):
# "ṛebɛa / ṛewɛa ; ar. S'il est suivi d'un nom, celui-ci est à l'ann. ‖ Quatre." "ṛebɛa warrac, quatre garçons."
# lang.json has the order "MARKER NUM UNIT" for this construction.
ussan
ass
wass
wussan
